                    "severity": "blocking",
                    "description": "High severity: unknown model usage does not fence session continuation. adapters/models/src/model-adapter.ts:34–36 preserves an unknown reservation, but engine/kernel/src/session-loop.ts:38 records no pending operation or waiting state when the model port rejects. The integrated model port in evals/protected/g0-workflows.test.ts:41 converts the unknown result into an exception, leaving the session running with no pendingOperations. Source-grounded reproduction using that fixture: create workflow(100,false,true), start its session, catch s.callModel('model-1'), then inspect s.nextAction(). It returns 'iterate'; s.callModel('model-2') reaches another provider invocation while reservation-model-1 remains unknown. An approved effect can likewise continue. This violates G0-IMP-04 and the required reconciliation-before-continuation ordering. Existing unknown-model recovery coverage checks reuse of the original operation directly through the adapter, but does not check session continuation. Backend owner should persist unknown model operation/reservation identity in session state, require trusted reconciliation before further iteration, preserve it through replay/restart, and add behavioral regression assertions without weakening frozen branches. Reproduction was derived from source, not executed.",
